00:01:31.930 --> 00:01:33.600
Now, back to the show.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:35.910
Now, "The Batman" shows
Gotham as a city where

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.850
lies and concealment are so common,

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:39.630
they're practically part
of the infrastructure.

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:40.920
On a most obvious level,

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:43.830
there's Batman's steadfast
refusal to view his identity

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.510
to anyone, even to a
fellow leather enthusiast.

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.720
- Who are you under there?

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.270
- But the shadowy edges of Gotham

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.200
are brought into sharp focus by the film's

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:53.030
also masked villain, The Riddler.

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.380
He repeatedly states his grand project,

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:57.600
to shine a light on all the city's lies.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.140
He's targeting the rich and powerful

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:00.460
for their various deceits,

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.180
which range from funding
sketchy nightclubs

00:02:02.180 --> 00:02:03.810
to faking a giant drug bust.

00:02:03.810 --> 00:02:06.970
And the most egregious deceit
is also the most widespread.

00:02:06.970 --> 00:02:08.300
The city's elite have straight up

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.840
looted the Gotham Renewal fund,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.420
which the Wayne family established to help

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:12.330
clean up the town.

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:15.070
And by the time we get to
the film's final, big reveal,

00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:17.140
that a mafia-esque kingpin is puppeteering

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.540
Gotham's entire government,

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.570
it's clear that these widely accepted lies

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:21.860
go all the way to the top.

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:23.900
All this deceit from the
city's rich and powerful

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:26.570
made us think of Plato's
concept of the noble lie.

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:28.857
As explored in a controversial
paragraph of his book,

00:02:28.857 --> 00:02:31.720
"The Republic," he explains
that rulers will need a throng

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:34.210
of lies and deceptions for
the benefits of the ruled.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.420
Basically, a noble lie is an untruth

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:38.350
that a society's leaders
use to persuade their

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.850
citizens to fall into line,

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:42.110
all in the name of keeping
their society functioning.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.520
A common noble lie is that
a given country's land

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.060
inherently belongs to its people,

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.050
even if that land was actually stolen.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.670
A simple way of thinking of a
noble lie is the way parents

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.260
might be dishonest with their
child for their own good.

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.720
Plato basically thought that
such lies could be justified

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.770
if they served moral ends and means.

00:02:57.770 --> 00:03:00.490
Modern philosophers like Leo
Straus have endorsed noble lies

00:03:00.490 --> 00:03:02.180
as necessary for social cohesion.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:04.610
It's good to keep people
united in their ideology,

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.830
even if that ideology
is falsely constructed.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.350
And we see a pretty perverted
version of the noble lie

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:11.840
in "The Batman" where a
government filled with apparently

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.030
good, honest leaders is revealed
to be a giant masquerade.

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:17.590
These leaders have long pretended
to be genuinely invested

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.660
in Gotham's Renewal, when in actuality,

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:22.420
the Wayne funds were treated
as a cash grab for corruption.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.920
The not so noble why,
that Thomas Wayne's funds

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.700
are being used to help the city flourish,

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:28.040
couldn't be further from the truth.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.910
Gotham's politicians
get to blame the city's

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:31.600
criminal underworld for all the crime

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.780
and economic problems,
while all the while,

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.940
working alongside those
very criminals to ensure

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.160
that they're both making
money hand over fist.

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:39.350
And it's effective.

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:41.920
The smoke and mirrors of the
Gotham Renewal Project and the

00:03:41.920 --> 00:03:44.070
lingering specter of
the criminal underworld

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.470
have kept the people
distracted while the select few

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:48.410
continue to enjoy their money and power.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.080
The lie has arguably
fostered social cohesion,

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.050
although probably not as effectively

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.810
as, say, actually investing
in your city's infrastructure

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.130
and social services, but hey, I digress.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.200
And throughout the movie,

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:02.170
we see more noble lies,
but on a smaller scale.

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:04.270
For example, we learned
that Batman's dad went

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:06.690
to great lengths to maintain
his wife's reputation.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:09.310
Eventually, this led him
to send a seedy crime boss

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.400
to intimidate an
investigative reporter who was

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.730
gonna publish a story about
the less savory details

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:15.030
of his wife's personal history.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:17.700
As usually happens when you
hire your local crime boss

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:20.050
for a freelance gig that
this resulted in murder,

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.900
all of which is sounding not super noble.

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.560
In tandem with this revelation,

00:04:24.560 --> 00:04:26.350
we also see that Batman's vision

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.210
of his father as the ultimate pinnacle

00:04:28.210 --> 00:04:31.000
of human goodness has
too been a noble lie.

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.460
Alfred admits that he didn't
tell Batman the truth about his

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:35.020
father because he knew little Bruce

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:36.380
desperately needed to believe in his

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:38.020
dad's unimpeachable greatness.

00:04:38.020 --> 00:04:40.410
Here, it's worth noting
a choice that strikes us

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.150
as the movie's biggest shortcoming,

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:44.380
its refusal to double down on sullying

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.900
the image of Thomas Wayne.

00:04:45.900 --> 00:04:48.890
See, at first, Batman thinks
that his dad intended to

00:04:48.890 --> 00:04:49.990
have the reporter killed,

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.870
a horrifying prospect that
would tarnish Thomas's legacy.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.840
However, he quickly learns that
all Thomas wanted to do was

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.990
scare the reporter, rather than kill him,

00:04:57.990 --> 00:04:59.600
all in the name of protecting his wife.

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.640
What's more, Thomas was racked
with guilt in the aftermath

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:03.510
of the murder.

00:05:03.510 --> 00:05:06.550
In fact, Alfred even says that
Thomas was planning to go to

00:05:06.550 --> 00:05:08.970
the police and that this
may have been the reason

00:05:08.970 --> 00:05:10.450
he himself was killed.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:13.060
This felt like a bit of a
cop-out and a missed opportunity

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.900
to really complicate the Wayne
legacy in an interesting way.

00:05:15.900 --> 00:05:19.210
Importantly, making Thomas
Wayne a capital B bad guy

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.360
would've created some nice
mirroring in the two threads

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:22.193
of the plot.

00:05:22.193 --> 00:05:24.110
We'd have to watch
Batman personally reckon

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:26.970
with the same thing the city
of Gotham is on a larger scale,

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:28.850
the fact that the people
they admired most were

00:05:28.850 --> 00:05:31.500
actually super sus and blatantly immoral.

00:05:31.500 --> 00:05:33.180
Instead, it's like everybody else got

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.680
Santa spoiled for them
while Batman just found out

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.030
that Santa made one really
bad choice in the '80s.

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:40.690
So, what happens when
noble lies become intrinsic

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.080
to a given society's functioning?

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:44.450
Kind of like your increasingly
elaborate explanation

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.920
about why you got home late from school,

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.660
which had nothing at
all to do with the eight

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:48.950
bong rips at Cory's house.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.710
Lies tend to beget more lies.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.050
A lie then about the
city's biggest drug bust

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:54.590
then begets another lie,

00:05:54.590 --> 00:05:56.630
that the busted drug
ring has been shut down,

00:05:56.630 --> 00:05:57.940
when in actuality,

00:05:57.940 --> 00:06:00.560
it's continued to flourish
by bribing public officials.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.940
And as The Riddler reveals
the total dishonesty

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:03.930
of each public figure,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.280
he starts to show how this
cycle of deceit has eaten

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.790
away at the foundation of
Gotham's civil society.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:09.840
By the end of the film,

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.600
we learned that just about
every powerful person employed

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:14.750
by the city of Gotham
has accommodated the lies

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:17.110
and corruption necessary
to maintain their of power.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.470
So, obviously, the rich
and influential are

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:22.250
super duper guilty, although
certainly not deserving

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:24.500
of having their faces devoured by rats.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.470
But by the end, The Riddler
becomes even more radical,

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.320
suggesting that all of Gotham
is culpable for blindly

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:32.540
accepting the lies fed
to them by politicians

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.610
and thus are complicit
in the creation of this

00:06:34.610 --> 00:06:35.780
deceitful society.

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:37.650
The film itself reflects some sense

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:38.990
of communal responsibility,

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:41.480
showing the solemn beginning
of a funeral for the mayor

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:43.550
where presumably nobody
was planning to mention

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:44.470
those leaked photos of him

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.080
with a young woman who had been battered.

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:47.870
But when Riddler escalates his attack

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.810
to target the entire city of Gotham,

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:51.720
things start feeling a little religious,

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.730
and not just because the song "Ave Maria"

00:06:53.730 --> 00:06:55.300
pops up at least twice in the film.

00:06:55.300 --> 00:06:56.960
See, by the Riddler's estimation,

00:06:56.960 --> 00:06:59.400
the sense of the city's
leaders, and consequently,

00:06:59.400 --> 00:07:00.870
its people are too heinous

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.200
for Gotham society to ever be redeemed.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.720
That's why he decides to flood
the whole place, ironically,

00:07:05.720 --> 00:07:06.940
by destroying some of the city's

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.490
actually functional infrastructure.

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:11.310
This can't help but make us
think of the Old Testament

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.530
God and the whole
flooding the goddamn world

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:15.520
because people were
behaving immorally thing.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:16.810
As if it wasn't harsh enough,

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.990
God additionally rained burning sulfur

00:07:18.990 --> 00:07:20.650
on the city of Sodom specifically

00:07:20.650 --> 00:07:22.650
for the reason The Riddler floods Gotham.

00:07:22.650 --> 00:07:24.780
It was a corrupt place
that failed to use its

00:07:24.780 --> 00:07:27.540
resources to take care of
its most vulnerable citizens.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:29.490
These evocations are anything but subtle.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:31.430
And don't even get us
started on the whole sins

00:07:31.430 --> 00:07:33.200
of the father theme
throughout the movie, too.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.350
But, back to The Riddler.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.190
He's a bad guy for a reason.

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.310
Where he sees an unredeemable society

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:40.110
or an unredeemable family,

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.230
Batman sees something else entirely.

00:07:42.230 --> 00:07:44.700
To understand, let's track
Batman's personal arc

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.533
in the film.

00:07:45.533 --> 00:07:47.960
He starts off really stoked
on the idea of vengeance,

00:07:47.960 --> 00:07:50.250
believing that the best
way to keep people safe is

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:53.430
by A, giving them
something to fear, and B,

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.190
making sure people are held accountable

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:56.970
for their actions with violence.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.070
He might not be drowning an entire city,

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:00.530
but this approach is not unlike

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:02.290
the Riddler's Old Testament vibes.

00:08:02.290 --> 00:08:03.400
But throughout the film,

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.580
this approach to making
society a better place

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:06.720
is called into question,

00:08:06.720 --> 00:08:08.810
not the least of which when
The Riddler tells Batman

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:10.460
that he has been an essential player

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:11.880
in the villain's deranged plot

00:08:11.880 --> 00:08:14.170
and even says that they
are basically teammates.

00:08:14.170 --> 00:08:17.210
But the validity of vengeance
as a guiding moral compass

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:20.390
is called into question
most explicitly when Batman

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:22.790
faces off against The Riddler's snipers

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.510
who have been shooting into a crowd.

00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:28.330
One of the snipers, when asked
his name, replies vengeance,

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:30.830
thus mirroring Batman's
ideology back at him.

00:08:30.830 --> 00:08:33.450
Obviously, sharing the same
mantra as a banana's group

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:35.160
of snipers isn't a good look,

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.500
so it's no surprise that
our hero ultimately settles

00:08:37.500 --> 00:08:38.370
on a different view.

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:40.770
He decides that rather than
needing someone to fear,

00:08:40.770 --> 00:08:43.710
the people of Gotham really
need someone to believe in,

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.060
someone to inspire hope.

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:47.850
And as he saves people from
The Riddler's giant flood,

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.540
Batman becomes that guy.

00:08:49.540 --> 00:08:52.570
In the process, he also reads
kind of like a Jesus figure

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.370
to The Riddler's Old Testament God,

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:57.040
the brave guy willing to
make enormous sacrifices

00:08:57.040 --> 00:08:59.610
and even risk death in
order to redeem a world

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:00.650
filled with sinners,

00:09:00.650 --> 00:09:03.460
someone who wants justice
more than he does vengeance.

00:09:03.460 --> 00:09:04.580
- The answer's justice

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.000
- But what do you guys think?

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.840
Can noble lies be a justifiable
way to keep any given

00:09:08.840 --> 00:09:10.100
society humming along?

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:12.350
Would you rather not know
just how deeply corrupt

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:13.460
the rich and powerful are?

